{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Bakewell&limit=10&title=At the Existentialist Café","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":[{"title":"At the existentialist café","subTitle":"freedom, being, and apricot cocktails with Jean-Paul Sartre, Simone de Beauvoir, Albert Camus, Martin Heidegger, Karl Jaspers, Edmund Husserl, Maurice Merleau-Ponty and others"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Existentialist café"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Existentialist café"}],"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["Bakewell, Sarah",{"@type":"date","#text":"1963-"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author."}}]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History."},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies."},{"@authority":"saogf","#text":"Biografi."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2016"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York :"}},"publisher":"Other Press,","dateIssued":[2016]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"439 pages : illustrations ; 24 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Paris, 1933. Three contemporaries meet over apricot cocktails at the Bec-de-Gaz bar on the rue Montparnasse-- and ignite a movement, creating an entirely new philosophical approach inspired by themes of radical freedom, authentic being, and political activism: Existentialism. Interweaving biography and philosophy, Bakewell provides an investigation into what the existentialists have to offer us today, at a moment when we are once again confronting the major questions of freedom, global responsibility, and human authenticity in a fractious and technology-driven world."},"tableOfContents":"Sir, what a horror, existentialism! -- To the things themselves -- The magician from Messkirch -- The they, the call -- To crunch flowering almonds -- I don't want to eat my manuscripts -- Occupation, liberation -- Devastation -- Life studies -- The dancing philosopher -- Croisés comme ça -- The eyes of the least favoured -- Having once tasted phenomenology -- The imponderable bloom.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Sarah Bakewell."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references (pages [339]-421) and index."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"e-fr---"}},{"@authority":"nli","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Sartre, Jean-Paul",{"@type":"date","#text":"1905-1980"}]}},{"@authority":"nli","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Beauvoir, Simone de",{"@type":"date","#text":"1908-1986"}]}},{"@authority":"nli","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Camus, Albert",{"@type":"date","#text":"1913-1960"}]}},{"@authority":"nli","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Heidegger, Martin",{"@type":"date","#text":"1889-1976"}]}},{"@authority":"nli","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Jaspers, Karl",{"@type":"date","#text":"1883-1969"}]}},{"@authority":"nli","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Husserl, Edmund",{"@type":"date","#text":"1859-1